result: 'P0-7 verified implemented: src/mir/verify.rs enforces block/terminator/dominance/operand/ret-type/phi
  invariants; wired into driver/mod.rs and driver/pipeline.rs post-lowering and post-Perceus.
  Added 11 hand-crafted broken-MIR unit tests (undefined value, ret-type mismatch,
  return-void from non-void, missing block, duplicate blocks, bad entry, multiply-defined
  value, phi from non-predecessor, non-truthy branch cond, fn-name in program errors,
  well-formed accept). All pass.'
description: 'Add a MIR verifier that runs after lowering and after each Perceus pass.
  Invariants to enforce: every block has a terminator; every used value has a dominating
  definition; operand types match operator signature (no pointer operand to integer
  arithmetic); declared function return type matches every Return terminator''s operand
  type. Under debug_assertions: panic with high-detail message. In release: tracing::error!
  + abort. Create `src/mir/verify.rs` and call it from the pipeline. Add `tests/mir_verifier.rs`
  with hand-crafted broken MIRs. This blocks P0-3 fix verification and prevents future
  IR corruption. (review/14_findings.md P0-7, review/15_roadmap.md A.1)'
